    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d856">

                <pb facs="1353" n="1339" xml:id="pg1339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/7–2944</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gore-Booth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Legal
                        Adviser</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hackworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-29">29 July, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hackworth</hi>: With reference to the
                    meeting which took place in your office on July 7th at which was discussed the
                    draft of a directive to Military commanders in the field on the subject of
                    treatment of war criminals, I am glad to inform you that we have now heard from
                    the Foreign Office that they approve the draft which we agreed on that
                    occasion.</p>
                <p>I am sending you two extra copies of this letter for your convenience in
                    informing the War and Navy Departments.</p>
                <p>This Embassy is also communicating with the British Secretariat of the Combined
                    Chiefs of Staff in order that preparations may be made for the issue of the
                    agreed directive provided that the final concurrence of the United States
                    Government authorities concerned is forthcoming.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul Gore-Booth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
